{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310773,"nonce":"P68WC5pDcSooAcJ0+FJTM94c8xk=","title":"Single (f32) SHIPPED 85d19b65; `extends` raw-bit id guess REPAIRED 1a8e672e. Root cause of the hang was UNGUARDED class-parent-chain walks ...","message":"Chasing `Single` end to end. Motivation: the Q4 band kernel is 77% SCALAR\ninstructions, and ~800 of them are f64 math + f32\u003c-\u003ef64 conversions, because\n`f16ToF32` and `q4DotBody` return Haxe `Float` (= f64) and store via\n`Mem.storeF32`.\n\n`Single` was `#if (java || cs || hl || cpp)` in StdTypes.hx — **conditionally\ncompiled OUT**, so `var s:Single` silently resolved to an opaque `*void` slot\ncarrying f64 bits. It ran, printed plausible numbers, and was a lie.\nProbe: `fn @takesSingle($0: *void) -\u003e *void` in `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1`.\n\n**RULE (user, verbatim): \"Don't remove other targets from stdlib. you should\nhave simply added rayzor to the list.\"** I deleted the whole `#if` guard.\nCorrect form is `#if (java || cs || hl || cpp || rayzor)`.\n\nEvery Haxe target defines its own name. rayzor only masqueraded as `eval` to\npick stdlib branches, so there was NO way to say \"this is rayzor\". Added\nunconditionally next to the `eval` insert. Use it for target-specific stdlib\nguards.\n\nUser: **\"You need to check codegen.\"** Each of these passed a MIR-type check\nand failed the LLVM verifier or produced wrong values:\n1. **`build_fma` hardcoded `llvm.fma.f64`** -\u003e `call double @llvm.fma.f64(float,\n   float, float)`. Poisons every downstream value; function fails verification\n   and the WHOLE PROGRAM silently drops to Cranelift.\n2. **float\u003c-\u003efloat width missing at 3 coercion sites** (phi, call args, binop\n   operands). All three handled int\u003c-\u003efloat only. `s + 1.0` built\n   `fadd float, double`.\n3. **`convert_to_string` registered the wrapper with the CALLER's type.** These\n   resolve BY NAME, so the first caller pinned the signature — one f32 arg made\n   `float_to_string` f32-taking and every later `Float` truncated. Printed\n   20.425 as 20.424999237060547. Pre-existing; Single merely exposed it.\n4. **String concat lost to the @:op rules**: `\"x=\" + v` with any abstract `v`\n   typed the expression as that abstract, so MIR called the concat (String ptr)\n   then cast that pointer float-\u003efloat.\n\n`build_class_vtables` walked `class_parent_map` in THREE places with a bare\n`while let Some(\u0026parent) = ...get(\u0026current)`, whose only exit is reaching a\nroot. `class_parent_map` comes from `extends` resolved partly by TypeId, and\nTypeIds are CONTEXT-LOCAL: declaring one more type shifts them and can make a\nclass its own ancestor. `PosException` did exactly that -\u003e infinite spin inside\nvtable construction, no output, no diagnostic.\n\nFix: `parent_chain()` helper that stops when the chain revisits a class; all\nthree sites use it. `collect_inherited_fields` got the same guard (93c4dcd1,\nkeyed on SymbolId which is stable) — that one removed a STACK OVERFLOW and\nEXPOSED this loop underneath. Two symptoms, one disease.\n\n`HirClass::extends` is **ambiguous by construction**: it holds EITHER a TAST\n`TypeId` resolvable via `type_table`, OR a symbol-derived\n`TypeId::from_raw(parent_sym.as_raw())` that tast_to_hir emits for\ncross-context stability. Consumers disambiguated by trying `type_table` and\n**otherwise REINTERPRETING THE RAW BITS as a SymbolId**. Both id spaces share\none integer range, so the guess can be wrong in EITHER direction; declaring one\nmore type shifts TypeIds and flips a latent collision on. `PosException` then\ngot a self-edge in `class_parent_map`.\n\nFix: `HirClass.extends_symbol: Option\u003cSymbolId\u003e`, resolved ONCE in tast_to_hir\nwhere the lookup is unambiguous. hir_to_mir uses it directly; the fallback is a\n`type_table` lookup ONLY — no raw-bit reinterpretation — and a self-parent edge\nis rejected rather than recorded.\n\n**Verified the cycle is GONE, not tolerated**: temporarily turned\n`parent_chain`'s guard into a hard `panic!` and the suite was 170/170 with the\noriginal trigger present. Guard kept as warn-once (an unbounded walk must never\nhang the compiler) but it no longer fires.\n\n**GENERAL LESSON: never recover an id by reinterpreting another id's raw bits.**\nIf two id spaces can occupy one field, carry the disambiguating identity\nexplicitly. [[feedback_fqn_first_resolution]], [[bugs_new_module_static_only_sigsegv]].\n\n1. `sample \u003cpid\u003e` during the hang -\u003e all frames in `lower_module` (release\n   inlines callees, so that is the FLOOR, not the answer).\n2. `eprintln!` phase markers around each phase of `lower_module` -\u003e last marker\n   printed was \"type metadata done\" with no \"vtables done\" =\u003e inside\n   `build_class_vtables`.\n3. grep that function for unbounded loops -\u003e three `while let` parent walks.\n`lldb -b -o run -o bt` named `collect_inherited_fields` for the earlier\nstack-overflow variant.\n\n    abstract RzProbeType {}                  -\u003e PASS\n    abstract RzConvProbe to Float from Float -\u003e HANG\n    abstract RzConvProbe from Float          -\u003e HANG\n    Int to Float (already shipped)           -\u003e fine, `to Float` innocent\nSo an implicit `from Float` rule was what perturbed ids enough to expose it.\n\n`evaluate_tokens` tested for `||`/`\u0026\u0026` BEFORE stripping parens and split without\ntracking nesting, so `(a \u0026\u0026 b)` split to `[LParen,a]` + `[b,RParen]`; the first\nfragment began with `(` and evaluated FALSE.\n\n**Every parenthesized condition satisfied by its FIRST term was wrong** —\n`#if (cpp || java)` was false on cpp; `\u0026\u0026` inside parens was false always.\n`#if (java || cs || hl || cpp || rayzor)` only worked because `rayzor` was LAST.\nReplaced with recursive descent (or -\u003e and -\u003e unary -\u003e primary). 4 regression\ntests. **This did NOT fix the StdTypes hang — it is an independent bug.**\n\nSingle is ENABLED. Lowering is in place\n(`name_str == \"Single\"` -\u003e `IrType::F32`, in the Abstract arm of\n`convert_type` next to Usize/Ptr/Ref/Box).\n\n- `fn @sk($0: f32, $1: f32, $2: f32) -\u003e f32` — real f32 params\n- **per-step f32 rounding PROVEN**: `16777216 + 1` ten times stays 16777216\n  while the f64 control reaches 16777226. Stronger than counting instructions —\n  f64-then-round would give 16777226.\n- literal narrowing exact: 1.2345678901234567 -\u003e 1.2345678806304932\n- 1e300 -\u003e inf; f64 path unaffected (0.1+0.2 still 0.30000000000000004)\n\nFix the Float\u003c-\u003eSingle cycle, re-enable, then measure whether f32 block-scale\nmath actually helps the Q4 kernel. **CAVEAT: that math is PER-BLOCK, the same\nfrequency class as the header/imin work that twice cut static counts and moved\nthe clock ZERO.** Measure before spending more.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `feature_single_f32_scalar` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}